WEBVTT

00:01.140 --> 00:03.310
<i>The Easton Magic Academy.</i>

00:03.850 --> 00:08.020
<i>A historic and prestigious school
that has produced</i>

00:08.020 --> 00:09.980
<i>numerous pillars of the magic realm.</i>

00:10.690 --> 00:13.570
<i>Of course, its entrance examination
is notoriously difficult.</i>

00:13.570 --> 00:15.990
<i>Not even 3% of the applicants
will be admitted.</i>

00:16.910 --> 00:22.000
<i>Only those with superior magical powers
will be able to open the gates of Easton.</i>

00:22.620 --> 00:25.540
<i>Only those
with superior magical powers...</i>

02:00.970 --> 02:04.430
<i>Let's see,
among this year's applicants are...</i>

02:06.810 --> 02:11.150
<i>A scion of established nobility, and then
the undersecretary's son from the Bureau of Magic.</i>

02:11.900 --> 02:14.780
<i>All the bigwigs of society, so to speak.</i>

02:15.190 --> 02:17.950
<i>Maintenance of wands
and reviewing of grimoires.</i>

02:17.950 --> 02:20.280
<i>They're devoting themselves to the exam.</i>

02:20.280 --> 02:26.160
It's only proper to have ambitious candidates
for a school as prestigious as ours.

02:33.040 --> 02:34.670
<i>What the...</i>

02:35.250 --> 02:36.840
<i>Huh? What's going on?</i>

02:36.840 --> 02:40.090
<i>We're starting an entrance exam
for a magic school now.</i>

02:40.090 --> 02:42.180
<i>Why is someone pumping iron?</i>

02:42.430 --> 02:45.600
<i>No, calm down.
Maybe I'm imagining things.</i>

02:45.600 --> 02:50.060
<i>This is a magic school.
Slackers like that would never be here.</i>

02:50.850 --> 02:53.810
<i>He's doing the invisible chair
while reading a fitness book!</i>

02:54.020 --> 02:58.320
<i>Does he even want to pass this exam?
At least read some books about magic!</i>

02:58.490 --> 03:01.820
Consumption of protein within 45 minutes
of training is the most basic of fundamentals.

03:01.820 --> 03:03.530
<i>And he's talking to himself!</i>
Consumption of protein within 45 minutes
of training is the most basic of fundamentals.

03:03.530 --> 03:03.820
<i>And he's talking to himself!</i>

03:03.820 --> 03:08.910
<i>And who are those guys behind him?
They're anything but inconspicuous!</i>

03:08.910 --> 03:11.290
Are you sure this will work?

03:11.290 --> 03:13.670
Mash can't use magic.

03:13.670 --> 03:15.960
You don't trust me and my plans?

03:16.170 --> 03:19.090
I made his scar
indistinguishable from a real one.

03:19.090 --> 03:21.680
I'm sure we'll get a kick outta this.

03:22.590 --> 03:23.800
<i>Oh, well.</i>

03:23.800 --> 03:27.100
<i>Slackers like that
will fail the exam anyway.</i>

03:27.430 --> 03:29.730
I wonder what the exam is like.

03:29.980 --> 03:32.140
I have to pass it, no matter
what it turns out to be.

03:32.520 --> 03:34.270
Greetings!

03:35.020 --> 03:38.360
Welcome to Easton Magic Academy.

03:43.030 --> 03:47.370
I am overseeing today's entrance examination.
My name is Claude Lucci.

03:47.910 --> 03:49.250
The pleasure's all mine.

03:49.500 --> 03:51.410
C-Claude Lucci!

03:51.410 --> 03:54.250
This year's seventh
best up-and-coming mage!

03:54.500 --> 03:58.500
He's said to have mastered countless
advanced spells despite his youth!

03:59.670 --> 04:01.760
<i>How exhilarating.</i>

04:01.760 --> 04:04.390
<i>Praise and worship me even more!</i>

04:04.840 --> 04:08.350
It must've been hot
coming out of the fire like that.

04:08.470 --> 04:10.520
<i>I'm definitely going to flunk him!</i>

04:10.810 --> 04:13.480
Now, let's start our first exam.

04:13.480 --> 04:15.020
Take your seats.

04:15.150 --> 04:16.150
Seats?

04:16.150 --> 04:17.520
There are no seats!

04:19.110 --> 04:20.230
What?

04:24.950 --> 04:26.870
- Desks just appeared!
- Amazing!

04:29.830 --> 04:32.250
- Wh-Whoa!
- I've never seen magic like this!

04:32.250 --> 04:33.750
No wonder they have
high hopes for this professor!

04:34.370 --> 04:37.920
You could've just taken us to a room
that was already set up.

04:38.170 --> 04:39.250
<i>I'll kill him.</i>

04:40.380 --> 04:41.590
<i>No matter.</i>

04:41.590 --> 04:44.880
<i>The acceptance rate
of this exam is three percent.</i>

04:44.880 --> 04:48.010
<i>There's no way
slackers like him will pass.</i>

04:48.390 --> 04:50.560
You have 30 minutes!

04:50.760 --> 04:53.270
Now, begin!

04:55.440 --> 04:57.400
<i>The test paper...</i>

04:57.520 --> 04:59.770
<i>The questions are squirming around?</i>

05:01.440 --> 05:06.070
<i>That's right, I have enchanted
the test papers with my magic.</i>

05:06.070 --> 05:12.660
<i>Thus, to pass this exam you need to dispel
the magic and properly line up the questions.</i>

05:12.790 --> 05:14.290
He'll never pull this off.

05:14.290 --> 05:17.420
Why'd I think
this would work the other day?

05:18.500 --> 05:20.670
Could you kindly stop moving?

05:26.220 --> 05:29.050
Kindly... stop moving.

05:31.010 --> 05:32.310
What?

05:32.890 --> 05:33.810
I finished.

05:34.600 --> 05:36.310
<i>That guy from earlier...</i>

05:36.600 --> 05:38.600
<i>I'm sure it's just
some random scribbles...</i>

05:42.690 --> 05:45.070
<i>It's aligned so perfectly.</i>

05:45.320 --> 05:48.660
He's making that boulder float so easily!

05:50.160 --> 05:52.830
Whoa! He's running on water!

05:53.120 --> 05:55.120
<i>From that point on, Mash...</i>

05:55.370 --> 05:57.210
<i>somehow found ways
to pass the tests.</i>

06:01.130 --> 06:04.340
<i>How can a slacker like that
still be here?</i>

06:04.340 --> 06:07.840
<i>That tasteless brat
who makes a mockery of me...</i>

06:08.300 --> 06:10.090
<i>Then I guess I must...</i>

06:10.340 --> 06:11.970
This is the next test!

06:12.640 --> 06:14.220
Hey, the ground again is...

06:21.560 --> 06:24.610
In the next test, you will solve this maze.

06:24.610 --> 06:26.990
Of course, this is no ordinary maze.

06:26.990 --> 06:29.990
There are various traps set within.

06:30.490 --> 06:32.620
You have 30 minutes!

06:32.620 --> 06:36.000
Reach the goal by the time limit,
and you pass!

06:36.120 --> 06:38.120
Now, begin!

06:39.210 --> 06:41.170
So I have to get to the goal area?

06:41.500 --> 06:43.500
Sounds pretty easy.

06:43.500 --> 06:44.590
Excuse me!

06:45.840 --> 06:48.470
Can I tag along with you?

06:51.050 --> 06:51.890
Why?

06:51.890 --> 06:54.050
Huh? Um...

06:54.050 --> 06:58.140
I think it'd be more efficient
if we worked together.

06:59.890 --> 07:00.900
Makes sense.

07:01.100 --> 07:03.810
Th-Thank you very much!

07:06.070 --> 07:09.780
I wonder what kind of traps
will be waiting for us?

07:13.120 --> 07:14.910
It hurts!

07:18.120 --> 07:20.040
This maze has imps!

07:20.160 --> 07:22.080
Please save me!

07:24.960 --> 07:28.050
Th-This ground is trying to grab us!

07:29.090 --> 07:31.380
Don't leave me behind!

07:36.850 --> 07:38.680
Please wait.

07:38.890 --> 07:43.060
Please don't leave me behind!

07:44.270 --> 07:47.190
What was that about efficiency?

07:49.440 --> 07:50.650
We have to hurry.

07:52.530 --> 07:53.950
Levios Cuffus!

07:57.740 --> 07:59.080
What are these?

07:59.700 --> 08:02.120
I'm sorry I deceived you
this whole time.

08:02.120 --> 08:05.330
There's a certain reason
I have to keep you away from the goal.

08:05.670 --> 08:07.210
What reason?

08:07.630 --> 08:10.090
I-I don't want to tell you,
that's why it's a certain reason!

08:11.880 --> 08:13.430
So I've been deceived?

08:13.430 --> 08:16.350
That's useless.
Human strength can't break...

08:16.800 --> 08:17.850
I'm sorry...

08:19.720 --> 08:21.850
but I have my own certain reason, too.

08:23.890 --> 08:24.850
Later.

08:28.820 --> 08:32.360
Th-This is bad!
I have to chase and stop him.

08:32.570 --> 08:34.740
Four legs in the morning.

08:37.990 --> 08:43.120
Two legs in the afternoon,
and three legs at night.

08:43.580 --> 08:45.370
What is this creature?

08:45.960 --> 08:49.130
This is totally
one of the dangerous ones.

08:50.250 --> 08:53.260
<i>It's only a test.
I'll use my magic and...</i>

08:59.510 --> 09:01.850
Answer my riddle.

09:03.140 --> 09:06.150
<i>Oh no. My knees gave out.</i>

09:06.480 --> 09:08.690
<i>Bad, really bad. This is a riddle?</i>

09:08.690 --> 09:10.270
<i>What's the answer?</i>

09:10.270 --> 09:14.650
<i>Four legs in the morning,
two at noon, three at night...</i>

09:15.030 --> 09:19.160
<i>Oh, this sucks. I'm panicking
and I can't think straight!</i>

09:19.240 --> 09:24.660
Time's up. Thou shalt be punished.

09:25.540 --> 09:26.710
Help...

09:27.750 --> 09:29.420
<i>That's not right.</i>

09:29.840 --> 09:34.170
<i>This truly is punishment
for selfishly deceiving others.</i>

09:35.090 --> 09:37.640
<i>I'm so terrible.</i>

09:38.260 --> 09:41.350
<i>I'm sorry, Mushroom Head.</i>

09:45.480 --> 09:46.810
Such a creature...

09:47.390 --> 09:48.940
can't possibly exist.

09:55.280 --> 09:59.570
Wh-Why did you bother
to come back and save me?

09:59.780 --> 10:00.820
Well...

10:01.660 --> 10:06.750
If your reason was similar to mine,
I'd kinda feel sorry for you.

10:09.250 --> 10:13.500
But it looks like
we won't make it in time from here.

10:14.090 --> 10:17.590
How do you think
I came here in an instant?

10:22.600 --> 10:24.600
<i>Time is almost up.</i>

10:24.600 --> 10:26.980
<i>Multiple traps
and the guardian of the labyrinth...</i>

10:26.980 --> 10:29.810
<i>And the student I recruited to stop him.</i>

10:29.810 --> 10:32.770
<i>Since I put in this much effort,
I'm sure he...</i>

10:33.480 --> 10:35.650
Hey, what's with that loud noise?

10:35.650 --> 10:37.360
Sounds like something is breaking!

10:37.570 --> 10:39.610
<i>Th-There's no way.</i>

10:39.740 --> 10:44.240
<i>These walls are one meter thick
and are impervious to all magic.</i>

10:46.120 --> 10:49.000
<i>The walls!</i>

10:53.000 --> 10:57.510
H-He trudged straight outta there!

11:00.590 --> 11:03.470
Quite a curious young man.

11:08.310 --> 11:10.520
Is that allowed?
Can he really do that?

11:10.690 --> 11:11.900
There's no way he can!

11:11.900 --> 11:13.150
That's cheating!

11:13.150 --> 11:15.020
Gimme a break!

11:15.020 --> 11:21.160
Go home! Go home! Go home!

11:22.820 --> 11:23.910
I want to go home.

11:24.070 --> 11:27.120
That's absurd.
It's no longer a labyrinth!

11:27.120 --> 11:28.290
Indeed.

11:28.290 --> 11:30.620
You're supposed to get lost
in a maze before exiting!

11:30.620 --> 11:31.540
Good point.

11:31.540 --> 11:33.130
What is a maze for you?

11:33.130 --> 11:34.170
Philosophy.

11:34.170 --> 11:38.880
Go home! Go home! Go home!

11:38.880 --> 11:43.300
P-Please stop! It wasn't his fault!

11:43.510 --> 11:44.550
Stop it!

11:45.010 --> 11:46.930
If you say anything, you'll regret it!

11:46.930 --> 11:49.560
I can still reconsider that promise for now.

11:49.850 --> 11:51.440
- I was...
- Hey!

11:51.810 --> 11:55.520
I was intentionally getting in his way
so he wouldn't reach the goal.

11:55.900 --> 11:57.820
Professor Lucci asked me to.

11:59.650 --> 12:03.450
He told me he would pass me
if I got in his way.

12:03.910 --> 12:08.330
My family is poor, and I desperately
wanted to be accepted for their sake.

12:08.660 --> 12:13.080
But he still saved me,
and then said to me,

12:13.460 --> 12:15.750
"Please marry me"!

12:15.750 --> 12:17.210
No, I didn't say that.

12:17.460 --> 12:18.840
I mean...

12:19.170 --> 12:21.340
If you're injured, I can piggyback you.

12:21.340 --> 12:24.260
Huh? Wait, that means...

12:24.430 --> 12:26.760
I'm a burden, you know?

12:27.890 --> 12:30.720
I don't really mind burdens at all.

12:32.850 --> 12:34.850
Don't be so bashful.

12:34.850 --> 12:38.400
I know how you really feel.

12:38.400 --> 12:41.240
It was really great. Yeah.

12:41.240 --> 12:43.860
No, I totally didn't say that.

12:45.280 --> 12:47.700
That's right. What about it?

12:47.700 --> 12:49.740
I'm the examiner.

12:49.740 --> 12:52.870
What's bad about trying
to fail students I don't like?

12:53.120 --> 12:55.880
A cheeky brat and a pauper girl.

12:56.040 --> 13:02.510
I reached out thinking even scum can be
useful, but you bit the hand that fed you.

13:02.920 --> 13:05.340
Is your stupidity
inherited from your parents?

13:05.340 --> 13:08.760
No wonder you have a miserable life.

13:12.350 --> 13:15.060
I'm failing you both.

13:15.350 --> 13:17.860
If you want to complain,
then challenge the decision.

13:17.860 --> 13:21.400
Challenge me,
a Magus Cum Laude Professor!

13:21.780 --> 13:25.570
Of course, that's only if you dare!

13:29.160 --> 13:31.330
That's going too far, Professor.

13:31.330 --> 13:33.080
What?

13:33.500 --> 13:36.370
Wow. He broke that wand.

13:36.370 --> 13:39.340
That's just the type of kid he is, huh?

13:39.590 --> 13:41.090
I kinda feel sorry for him.

13:41.210 --> 13:43.800
Shut up! Why would I even—

13:43.800 --> 13:45.090
Silence!

13:48.300 --> 13:50.350
Headmaster Wahlberg.

13:50.550 --> 13:53.600
We will now begin the final interviews.

13:53.720 --> 13:56.980
From this point on,
I will take charge of the examination.

13:57.190 --> 13:59.860
Headmaster, why are you here?

14:00.060 --> 14:01.360
Lucci.

14:02.020 --> 14:05.360
See me in my office after this.

14:05.780 --> 14:08.410
A-As you wish.

14:09.320 --> 14:12.620
Now, let's start with our first applicant.

14:19.710 --> 14:24.630
We will now begin the final interview
for Mash Burnedead.

14:25.670 --> 14:27.510
Thank you for having me.

14:27.840 --> 14:32.390
First, let's hear
why you chose our academy.

14:38.640 --> 14:42.650
To live in peace with my family.

14:42.820 --> 14:44.480
That's not an answer.

14:44.480 --> 14:45.860
What does that mean?

14:45.860 --> 14:47.650
It's fine.

14:47.900 --> 14:49.530
Next question.

14:49.660 --> 14:55.410
Is it true that you saved a girl in the maze test,
although you didn't have time to?

14:56.040 --> 14:57.660
I guess so.

14:57.660 --> 15:03.040
What made you do so,
even by risking to fail the test?

15:03.540 --> 15:05.960
I kinda felt like I would regret it.

15:08.470 --> 15:13.510
You seem to be the type
who acts before thinking.

15:13.510 --> 15:16.850
You never considered
that the sphinx might be stronger,

15:16.850 --> 15:21.810
or that you may not be able
to break the walls?

15:22.060 --> 15:25.480
Well, even if I considered,
it still had to be done.

15:28.320 --> 15:30.200
Extremely amusing.

15:30.450 --> 15:36.740
But you can only say that because
you don't understand the ways of the world yet.

15:36.740 --> 15:40.580
Many creatures that are stronger
than you exist in this world.

15:41.040 --> 15:45.750
If you were to face something
that overwhelmingly outpowers you,

15:45.750 --> 15:49.880
would you still be able
to take the same course of action?

15:51.090 --> 15:53.340
Even if you were...

15:59.640 --> 16:01.850
facing me?

16:03.560 --> 16:05.730
<i>What immense magical power.</i>

16:06.020 --> 16:08.230
<i>And this spell!</i>

16:12.950 --> 16:14.370
What is this?

16:14.530 --> 16:23.620
This is an ancient spell that transfers the soul
of the target's most cherished one into a doll.

16:24.920 --> 16:25.750
Gramps?

16:25.960 --> 16:28.250
What's wrong? Gramps! Hey!

16:28.670 --> 16:31.380
Of course, that's not all.

16:31.380 --> 16:34.890
If I were to stab a knife
into the soulful doll...

16:35.010 --> 16:37.760
that being would never return.

16:44.770 --> 16:46.270
Didn't I already tell you?

16:46.770 --> 16:50.650
I am immensely more powerful than you.

16:50.730 --> 16:54.450
You can't do anything in your current state.

16:54.820 --> 16:59.160
And in a situation like this,
what would you...

17:06.580 --> 17:10.300
You can't keep something
this huge out forever.

17:11.170 --> 17:14.050
This is an endurance contest, right?

17:19.560 --> 17:24.060
Power can be used to harm or to help.

17:24.390 --> 17:28.230
It all depends
on the wielder of that power.

17:28.940 --> 17:32.440
That is the reason why I put emphasis...

17:32.990 --> 17:36.450
on protecting the weak,
and regulating the strong.

17:36.780 --> 17:42.540
Noblesse Oblige.
One's capacity as a powerful being.

17:43.500 --> 17:51.250
And according to my observations,
you are a human who possesses that capacity.

17:58.300 --> 18:00.180
My apologies.

18:00.180 --> 18:03.520
I was literally testing you.

18:03.930 --> 18:06.850
I had no intention of that nature.

18:07.440 --> 18:08.940
Don't worry about it.

18:11.230 --> 18:12.730
What is it?

18:13.150 --> 18:15.070
What you asked earlier, Headmaster.

18:15.070 --> 18:20.030
The answer to the question
"If I had to face the Headmaster..."

18:21.080 --> 18:23.910
If it comes to that,
I'd knock the stuffing out of you...

18:23.910 --> 18:25.000
with my fist.

18:27.460 --> 18:28.790
What insolence!

18:28.790 --> 18:30.380
Are you insane?

18:33.210 --> 18:37.420
Welcome to Easton Magic Academy.

18:39.340 --> 18:41.010
Are you okay, old man?

18:41.430 --> 18:43.100
Be gentle with me.

18:43.560 --> 18:45.640
<i>And so, a lot of things happened.</i>

18:46.350 --> 18:51.650
<i>But Mash Burnedead passed the entrance exam
for Easton Magic Academy.</i>

18:52.400 --> 18:56.650
Today, we will be learning one of the most
basic of spells, the lock-opening spell.

18:57.030 --> 19:00.490
You must imagine opening the lock
as you infuse it with magic energy.

19:00.490 --> 19:01.660
Opti Ars.

19:04.330 --> 19:06.660
Now, let's actually try it.

19:10.000 --> 19:11.210
Professor. I opened it.

19:14.710 --> 19:19.550
Why you little, that's not...
That's not it at all, damn it!

19:19.550 --> 19:21.390
This is a magic school, you know?

19:21.390 --> 19:23.850
A place where you learn magic!

19:23.850 --> 19:25.430
Well, I...

19:26.850 --> 19:28.770
I'm not good with magic and the like.

19:28.770 --> 19:30.440
Why are you even here?

19:31.100 --> 19:33.150
Looks like I have a hard path ahead.

19:33.150 --> 19:35.360
Why are you sounding like
it's not your business?

19:35.360 --> 19:37.570
What kind of nerves do you have?

19:37.820 --> 19:40.650
<i>What's with this year's transfers?</i>

19:40.650 --> 19:43.570
<i>There's someone who's clearly bad news!</i>

19:43.910 --> 19:45.120
God is dead.

19:45.120 --> 19:45.870
Where the hell did that come from?
Seriously creepy!

19:45.870 --> 19:48.200
<i>I definitely don't want to be around him.</i>
Where the hell did that come from?
Seriously creepy!

19:48.450 --> 19:49.960
Where are you looking at now?

19:49.960 --> 19:52.960
Listen! Listen to what others have to say!

19:55.210 --> 19:57.510
<i>Since this is a boarding school...</i>

19:57.840 --> 20:01.260
<i>I really don't want to be roommates
with people like that.</i>

20:01.630 --> 20:04.260
Let's see, my room...

20:05.010 --> 20:06.220
Huh, wait...

20:06.470 --> 20:07.770
The door...

20:14.650 --> 20:17.820
I'm Finn Ames.
Nice to be rooming with you.

20:20.440 --> 20:22.570
I'm Mash Burnedead.

20:22.820 --> 20:27.540
I don't really know a lot, so I might
cause trouble, but it's nice to room with you.

20:27.620 --> 20:29.870
<i>Huh? He's surprisingly normal?</i>

20:30.000 --> 20:32.370
And this is Kevin.

20:33.120 --> 20:34.920
This one's Mike.

20:35.170 --> 20:40.550
<i>This guy names his muscles! Freaky!
And when did he change clothes?</i>

20:41.130 --> 20:45.590
W-Well, you can ask me
anything you don't know.

20:45.590 --> 20:50.180
The dorm pairs up transfers and continuing
students together as roommates.

20:50.180 --> 20:52.690
It's customary to help each other out.

20:53.270 --> 20:54.690
I see.

20:54.690 --> 20:56.310
<i>Be nice for now.</i>

20:56.310 --> 20:58.860
<i>Nice, and distant.</i>

20:58.980 --> 21:01.860
<i>This is for a peaceful school life.</i>

21:02.110 --> 21:03.490
Can I ask you one thing?

21:03.490 --> 21:04.200
Sure.

21:04.950 --> 21:08.780
How do you get to be
the academy's "Divine Visionary"?

21:08.780 --> 21:10.700
Oh, a Divine Visionary?

21:11.040 --> 21:13.120
You have to collect gold coins.

21:13.120 --> 21:18.790
Tests, coursework, extracurriculars, school life.
We're evaluated on everything.

21:18.790 --> 21:23.090
Based on the evaluations, you're given
coins of gold, silver, or bronze.

21:23.510 --> 21:25.930
Regardless of coins earned,

21:25.930 --> 21:30.350
if you can't keep your grades up
each semester, you'll be expelled.

21:30.970 --> 21:35.020
I had a vague feeling,
but this is really brutal.

21:35.020 --> 21:37.350
<i>Looks like he'll be expelled real quick.</i>

21:37.560 --> 21:39.940
So that's why we're all desperate.

21:39.940 --> 21:41.360
Including me, of course.

21:41.690 --> 21:43.240
Best of luck to you, too.

21:43.240 --> 21:47.360
<i>Finn made sure not to say,
"Let's do our best together."</i>

21:47.660 --> 21:49.620
You're a great guy.

21:49.620 --> 21:52.330
<i>And Mash was very simple.</i>

21:52.450 --> 21:54.080
You want a cream puff?

21:54.370 --> 21:56.830
Huh? Where did you pull those out of?

21:56.830 --> 21:58.250
I'll take one, though.

21:59.170 --> 22:03.880
<i>Will Mash with no magical powers
really be able to become the Divine Visionary?</i>
